Z||000046||BlackStang95||11-08-2001||01:33 PM||||Would someone please explain to me exactly how wealthy this guy may or may not have been has any bearing on some little sh!t stealing from him? Does that mean I can go steal Bill Gate's car because his net worth is so much greater than my own? Would you please explain where this line is drawn so I know who I can steal from and still maintain a clear conscience?<BR>Yeah, that's what thought. <P>It goes back to robin hood and all I guess, stealing from rich to give to poor.  Although im sure those kids hardly needed and valve caps, you seem to have gotten it all wrong.<P>Theres no doubt those little punks were wrong and needed a hell of a lot of punishment, i totally agree with everything except he kept messing with them even after he knew he was gonna get more than compensated for his valve caps.  By responding the way he did he sunk way down to their 12 year old (or younger) level.  It's the parents job to correct kids, and the police if it goes beyond that.  I remember when i was about 13 this punk 10 year old was messing with me and i kicked his ass really bad, his dad came over and started talking **** , saying he would beat me up.  I went straight home and told my dad and he went over and got all up in the other dudes face until he backed down.  You don't discipline other peoples kids.  Theres a fine line between justice and bullying because youre a small person.  I know theres no one on this forum that can say they never did something stupid as a kid but we were lucky enoguh to not be crucified for it.  In short, no doubt they were wrong, but punishment should fit the crime.  <P>And i did have my car keyed once, so its not like i cant relate.  If i found out who it was I would surely have beat them up if they were old enough but if they were kids id just have told the parents and gotten a check $$.  ||||reg||1
