Z||000048||BlackStang95||11-08-2001||01:39 PM||||This was gonna be a pm to rogergarrison but its not letting me do it, ignore this unless your rodg.<P>You seem to have it all wrong, I'd never mess with someones car, thats cowardly and gay, i'd get in your damn face and tell you what i thought of you.  Guns are great equalizers unless the other guy/s has/have one too.  I do if you were wondering.  They don't make you invincible.  I never had a problem with you before but I didnt like your laughable attempt at a threat.  All i was trying to do was picture that kid as my own, i always see both sides of stories because im open minded, you should try it.  Peace.  ||||reg||1
Z||000049||BN Boomer||11-08-2001||01:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>It goes back to robin hood and all I guess, stealing from rich to give to poor.  Although im sure those kids hardly needed and valve caps, you seem to have gotten it all wrong.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So what are saying, that if I really NEED a car it's okay to be "Robin Hood" and steal one from a rich guy? Boy, you are really f@#$ed up.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>Theres no doubt those little punks were wrong and needed a hell of a lot of punishment<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, then, what's yer freakin' problem? You say this and then you go blathering about how the guy was too mean, a jerk, a bully. Maybe he should have just given the kid a hug and asked him not to do it again, huh? That "catch and release" policy seems to have proven a pretty effective tactic, right?<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>You don't discipline other peoples kids.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Which explains why there are so few behavorial problems in schools these days. Frankly, I think a good crack on the a** would do a lot of kids some good these days.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>I know theres no one on this forum that can say they never did something stupid as a kid but we were lucky enoguh to not be crucified for it.  In short, no doubt they were wrong, but punishment should fit the crime.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>These kids WERE NOT crucified and the punishment DID fit the crime. <P>In the end, you're not even a parent so this is purely academic for you. You have no real idea what it is like to be a parent. If this was one of my kids, I wouldn't have had any problems with the guy's actions and the kid would have been grounded, given extra chores,