Z||000067||Indy-2M4||11-09-2001||05:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>  You don't discipline other peoples kids.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That'a a load of crap!<P>It's gotta start with the parents and if the parents don't teach them right from wrong,  they just go on stealing. Again, what happens if SOMEONE doesn't discipline the brat? Snowball effect..he'll be snatching entire cars when he's older. Yeah, it's a dirty job, but if that little b----rd was stealing from me, I'd done about the same thing.<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR>F.K.A. KathyHL<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://sofa.iwarp.com/IndyFiero2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000068||DRH||11-09-2001||09:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B> I dunno 'bout you, but I probably would have learned that stealing valve stem covers wasn't really worth it.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>More likely he learned that guy is a jerk that deserves to have his stuff taken/vandalized.<P>If he had handled it better I might agree. Not only did he overstep his bounds, he did a piss poor job of it.||||reg||1
Z||000069||BN Boomer||11-09-2001||10:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DRH:<BR><B> More likely he learned that guy is a jerk that deserves to have his stuff taken/vandalized.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>If that is true, it's only because the kid obviosly has not been disciplined enough in life and the one time he does have his feet held to the fire for his behavvior he chooses to rationalize the consequences in a piss-poor manner like that.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000070||Voytek||11-09-2001||11:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>Just to put in my 2c:<P>A thief is a thief, but a kid is a kid. At this age, you are leaving impressions that will never go away. And the impression he will have from this incident is that he was punished waaaaaay too severe for the crime committed. Trust me. The guy did not do a good thing. Ask any psychologist.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Like I've said in my other reply, I do think the guy went just a bit far.  I do disagree with you, Cliff, on the 'kid is a kid' comment.  Where does 'a kid is a kid' become 'a kid is a criminal'?  Where is the line?  A lot of crimes are being committed by kids these days and justified by the phrase 'oh, they're just kids'.  For example, last month a 13 year old girl was charged with stabbing a boy with a knife in Calgary.  I mean, we've all done this, right at one point, right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> Where do you draw the line?<P>I believe you draw the line RIGHT from the start: right is right and wrong is wrong.  As far as I'm concerned there is no MORE right just because it's a kid.  He or she has the capacity to understand reason.  You can teach a dog not to poop in your house - you should definitely be able to teach your kids not to steal.<P>Someone mentioned parents disciplining their own kids.  Apparently these parents haven't conveyed the message that stealing is wrong.  And yes, the boy was old enough to understand this.<P>Also, Cliff, what psychologists are you talking about?  Would that be the same ones that speak out agains spanking your own kids for fear of emotional scarring?  Would it be the same ones that say kids should only be praised and never, ever scolded?  My point is most psychologists are messed in the head now days.<P>If parents don't teach right from wrong, someone else will (in some cases that won't happen till it's jail time).||||reg||1
Z||000071||Leadfoot||11-09-2001||11:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jake_Dragon:<BR><B>Is that EdsB52   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.contrabandent.com/pez1/otn/laughing/yelrotflmao.gif"> <P>||||reg||1
